WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:07.264
Aircraft return to the air, ships remain available at sea, and safety-critical
engineering moves forward because authorised people can

00:07.264 --> 00:10.175
show which source and revision governs the work.

00:10.175 --> 00:16.726
The physical outcome may be a released maintenance task, an accepted
engineering change or a resolved assurance question.

00:16.726 --> 00:24.368
Before any of those decisions, someone has to trace the requirement, inspect
the evidence and identify what is missing or inconsistent.

00:24.368 --> 00:30.190
Cortessa is designed to support that investigation without taking the decision
away from the accountable person.

00:31.190 --> 00:34.453
A technical approval rarely depends on one document.

00:34.453 --> 00:39.756
Requirements connect to engineering instructions, maintenance publications,
supplier evidence, standards, safety material and

00:39.756 --> 00:40.572
configuration records.

00:40.572 --> 00:45.874
Those sources may be owned by different teams and held in disconnected
environments.

00:45.874 --> 00:53.625
The assurance problem is establishing which source is current, whether every
reference is present, whether terminology still aligns and

00:53.625 --> 00:58.111
whether the evidence applies to the platform and task under review.

00:58.111 --> 01:00.151
Search can find a page.

01:00.151 --> 01:04.230
Assurance requires the route between the pages to remain inspectable.

01:05.230 --> 01:11.692
The credible starting point is one bounded technical-assurance workflow: for
example, a selected engineering-change or

01:11.692 --> 01:12.553
maintenance-release pack.

01:12.553 --> 01:18.584
Agree the authoritative corpus, revision set, expected source routes and
questions before testing begins.

01:18.584 --> 01:25.045
Define the existing baseline, the evidence standard and the authorised
engineers who will adjudicate results.

01:25.045 --> 01:28.492
Use only public, synthetic or explicitly cleared material.

01:28.492 --> 01:37.968
Cortessa is evaluated inside that fixed scope; it does not claim access to an
entire Defence estate or understanding of every platform

01:37.968 --> 01:38.830
and programme.

01:39.830 --> 01:44.447
Cortessa runs on a dedicated sovereign workstation inside the agreed boundary.

01:44.447 --> 01:51.163
The approved corpus, ingestion pipeline, local index, on-device model and
source viewer remain on that machine.

01:51.163 --> 01:55.360
Runtime operation does not depend on a public cloud service.

01:55.360 --> 01:59.978
The organisation controls the permitted documents, users, identity and
security posture.

01:59.978 --> 02:02.916
Retrieval-only operation remains available as the floor.

02:02.916 --> 02:11.311
Cortessa supports review inside the existing environment; it does not widen
access, connect to a platform or replace the organisation's

02:11.311 --> 02:12.150
information-governance controls.

02:13.150 --> 02:16.579
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

02:16.579 --> 02:23.438
It works across the bounded defence corpus rather than waiting for one
question at a time.

02:23.438 --> 02:29.440
It can surface missing references, supersession questions, revision
uncertainty, terminology differences and structured conflicts.

02:29.440 --> 02:35.870
Each candidate enters engineering review; it is not automatically a
certification, safety or compliance finding.

02:36.870 --> 02:41.433
Every audit result leads back to the passages that created it.

02:41.433 --> 02:47.241
The engineer can open the source, inspect surrounding wording and check
revision and applicability.

02:47.241 --> 02:52.220
If evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:52.220 --> 03:00.102
The engineer decides whether the issue is real, irrelevant, already controlled
or worth further investigation, then records the outcome

03:00.102 --> 03:01.761
through the existing process.

03:01.761 --> 03:05.910
Verified shows provenance; it does not decide which requirement governs.

03:06.910 --> 03:11.171
Technical authority cannot be outsourced to a language model.

03:11.171 --> 03:16.379
Configuration, applicability, safety significance and operational consequence
require authorised professional judgement.

03:16.379 --> 03:21.113
Cortessa makes the source route, provenance state and uncertainty visible.

03:21.113 --> 03:28.215
The responsible engineer resolves the issue and records the decision through
the organisation's approved process.

03:28.215 --> 03:35.790
Cortessa does not become the design authority, configuration authority, safety
authority, certifying body or procurement authority.

03:36.790 --> 03:38.912
Reviewers need more than an answer.

03:38.912 --> 03:45.280
They need the source route, document state and the policy governing what the
system is allowed to present.

03:45.280 --> 03:50.586
Identity, document currency, assertion policy and egress posture are visible
parts of the operating picture.

03:50.586 --> 03:57.307
Local activity can be recorded in a ledger so the organisation can inspect
what the system did and when.

03:57.307 --> 04:00.490
That record may contribute to an assurance evidence package.

04:00.490 --> 04:06.150
It does not make conclusions correct and does not replace the formal
engineering or approval record.

04:07.150 --> 04:10.623
Compare matched tasks against the existing review baseline.

04:10.623 --> 04:18.438
Measure time to locate and open the governing source, reviewer effort, cited
candidate findings, accepted and rejected results,

04:18.438 --> 04:21.911
appropriate refusals and reproducibility of sampled source paths.

04:21.911 --> 04:28.857
For aircraft support, test whether stale or missing evidence becomes visible
earlier in the selected review.

04:28.857 --> 04:34.935
For naval engineering, test the route from a candidate finding to its
governing source.

04:34.935 --> 04:39.277
For safety-critical assurance, test whether the conclusion-to-source trail is
clearer.

04:39.277 --> 04:42.750
These are evaluation hypotheses, not claimed operational outcomes.

04:43.750 --> 04:45.530
Bring one bounded workflow.

04:45.530 --> 04:49.090
Agree the corpus, reviewers, baseline and evidence standard.

04:49.090 --> 04:53.540
Include difficult scans, tables, ambiguous references and deliberately absent
evidence.

04:53.540 --> 04:57.990
Record setup and corpus-preparation effort as part of the result.

04:57.990 --> 05:04.220
Cortessa claims no Defence deployment, platform integration, accreditation,
approval, achieved saving or readiness outcome.

05:04.220 --> 05:08.670
The value has to be demonstrated in a representative environment.

05:08.670 --> 05:12.230
Start a conversation about a scoped Defence evaluation.
